{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "007G", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-stalk-abelian-presheaf}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5625ee51b2db9069a675133860300a35fcdeada570e1ea870f7b3c2945467fa8", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe proof of Lemma <REF_0001> will work\nfor any type of algebraic structure such that directed\ncolimits commute with the forgetful functor.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:840c598292d32fb4b29e287fb2c5123aeee70359b5202ebed51fa5d1aa57a8de", "unit_id": "tag:007G:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "007G", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$F : \\mathcal{C} \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0003": "$F$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$F$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0010": "$$\n\\mathcal{F}_x = \\colim_{x\\in U} \\mathcal{F}(U)\n$$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{F} \\mapsto \\mathcal{F}_x$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-stalk-presheaf-values-in-category}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ed8dc8319ac2292658c1f27df610ab0f4150cc00e1088931ebf13b24106c50c8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1156f22e4afd731f714ceb98597ae4d2bdb719a9278925c7e2897c021f38865e", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a category. Let <MATH_0002>\nbe a functor. Assume that\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0003> is faithful, and\n<STRUCT_0003> directed colimits exist in <MATH_0004> and <MATH_0005> commutes with\nthem.\n<STRUCT_0004>\nLet <MATH_0006> be a topological space. Let <MATH_0007>. Let <MATH_0008>\nbe a presheaf with values in <MATH_0009>.\nThen\n<MATH_0010>\nexists in <MATH_0011>. Its underlying set is equal to the\nstalk of the underlying presheaf of sets of <MATH_0012>.\nFurthermore, the construction <MATH_0013>\nis a functor from the category of presheaves with values in\n<MATH_0014> to <MATH_0015>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:51a91d06ed1fad6a3dbfaa91de9c81bbb8f9c6a6f08a0bdb1589c7c1cd4567df", "unit_id": "tag:007H:statement"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "007G", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2099312cfe070a896e5d6794de752281176ee2e8687bb2c2ac7f3263aaff5b4c", "source_text": "Omitted.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:872a8cfa74892c6e6464bd864d9f1c292f4f523caba3e51ac3dafbfc84db48f6", "unit_id": "tag:007H:proof"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "007G", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}(U)\n\\to \\mathcal{F}_x$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$F$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$F$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3c1483877f75f4ad52f6af2d5fbfc4837073dde31ee827274239922447badca3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b435183fc89716920525f42aca9210797840f19b6744366603fcc10631b89bb3", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nBy the very definition, all the morphisms <MATH_0001> are morphisms in the category <MATH_0002>\nwhich (after applying the forgetful functor <MATH_0003>) turn into\nthe corresponding maps for the underlying sheaf of sets.\nAs usual we will not distinguish between the morphism\nin <MATH_0004> and the underlying map of sets, which\nis permitted since <MATH_0005> is faithful.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nThis lemma applies in particular to:\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>Presheaves of (not necessarily abelian) groups, rings, modules\nover a fixed ring, vector spaces over a fixed field<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d91a20ca46923ed7af1dbf485e92e3d400a51ba038ee4630418469accf17ddf8", "unit_id": "tag:007G:prose-0002"}
